  "bounded_scenario": [
    "Before opening its persistent desk, actual PencilKit synthetic in-memory preflight checks initial hidden/read-only mounts preserve original stored ink and do not create an erasure; changed active-tool drawing captured exactly once on hide with original version and parent retained. This is framework lifecycle evidence, not hardware Pencil input.",
    "Exercise unchanged production ReadingDeskView inside a QA-only explicit 740/940-point width wrapper, with an original synthetic EPUB and the existing isolated QA desk. No user library or account source is opened.",
    "Final strict assertions find no THE BOOK label and zero native WebViews in the hidden reader XCTest snapshot; the hidden notebook label is absent while Book is selected.",
    "Set reading text to 21 points, enable markup mode, change chapter, switch Notebook/Book and widen the desk: chapter, font preference, and reader markup mode remain.",
    "Focus the actual native text editor, then narrow with Book selected. The captured native editing-end notification reports Notebook unfocused; the reader chapter/markup state remains.",
    "Open the EPUB/PDF file picker and cancel: no reader error is displayed and the selected book remains usable.",
    "Terminate and reopen the isolated app: font preference and saved chapter recover in the UI with no reader error. The test finally reopens the full QA app outside the width harness."
  ],
